     1	# COORDINATION.md — the campaign protocol
     2	
     3	This file owns the campaign's live operating policy. It is model-agnostic:
     4	any sufficiently capable model can fill any role below. Avenue inventory and
     5	ranking belong in `APPROACHES.md`; the detailed Keller-to-book / `G2-PSC` /
     6	`G2-BD` dependency map belongs in `ladder/REDUCTION.md`; claim-level evidence
     7	belongs in `AUDIT.md`. None is duplicated here.
     8	
     9	## Mission and decision rule
    10	
    11	Resolve the plane Jacobian conjecture, by proof or counterexample, as quickly
    12	as sound research permits. Urgency changes scheduling, not standards. Review
    13	gates promotion, publication, expensive commitment, and irreversible action;
    14	it does not normally block cheap, reversible research based on a result that
    15	has passed the provisional gate below.
    16	
    17	The coordinator may take routine, reversible actions within the campaign.
    18	External communication, publication, destructive operations, disclosure of a
    19	private result, and newly expensive commitments remain human decisions unless
    20	the human has granted standing authority for the exact action.
    21	
    22	## Canonical files and write ownership
    23	
    24	The six top-level Markdown files have disjoint jobs:
    25	
    26	- `README.md` — short project orientation and public-progress pointer.
    27	- `COORDINATION.md` — live process, roles, gates, clocks, and bootstrap.
    28	- `APPROACHES.md` — canonical avenue inventory and comparative ranking:
    29	  routes, gaps, promise, and tried/untried status.
    30	- `AUDIT.md` — promoted-claim and trust-boundary ledger, including
    31	  corrections. Promotion requires the review rule below.
    32	- `PROGRESS.md` — one compact digest per calendar day, newest first.
    33	- `notes.md` — append-oriented tick log and active-state journal.
    34	
    35	The newest `LIVE STATE` block in `notes.md` is authoritative for lanes, holds,
    36	provisional claims, review debt, clocks, and the immediate queue. `xmodel/`
    37	holds immutable producer, reviewer, sweep, and round reports; code and replay
    38	artifacts live beside the relevant cases. `ops/FLEET.md` owns machine inventory
    39	and compute safety rules.
    40	
    41	Do not maintain a second live queue, avenue map, or evidence ledger. Link to
    42	the canonical entry instead of copying it. When a digest must repeat a fact,
    43	label its date and evidence/lifecycle state; later corrections supersede but do
    44	not erase the historical record.
    45	
    46	## Roles
    47	
    48	Exactly one coordinator is active. A handoff becomes effective only after the
    49	outgoing coordinator banks an atomic `LIVE STATE` and the incoming coordinator
    50	acknowledges its basis; research and review lanes may otherwise remain active.
    51	
    52	- **Coordinator / integrator** — owns the scientific schedule and global
    53	  synthesis. It freezes round inputs, keeps the claim and avenue dependencies
    54	  legible, allocates capacity, adjudicates conflicting reports, attacks the
    55	  hardest integrative gap, banks state, and surfaces human-only decisions. The
    56	  strongest available reasoner should spend most of its time here or on the
    57	  one problem for which global context has the highest marginal value, not on
    58	  routine replay or documentation.
    59	- **Research lane** — one bounded prove, disprove, compute, implement, or
    60	  survey task. It names its input claims and permitted assumptions, owns its
    61	  task end-to-end, and writes one `xmodel/<tag>.md` report plus replayable
    62	  artifacts when applicable. It does not edit shared ledgers.
    63	- **Adversarial reviewer** — independently tries to break one claim by source
    64	  comparison, counterexample search, and direct replay. It reports a verdict
    65	  for each exact claim: `CONFIRMED`, `REFUTED`, or `GAP`, with the attack and
    66	  computation shown. It must not be the producer model.
    67	- **External-intelligence lane** — searches broadly for new results, actors,
    68	  artifacts, corrections, and priority changes; snapshots exact sources and
    69	  maps actionable items into campaign claims and avenues.
    70	- **Software / compute lane** — improves instruments or runs registered
    71	  experiments. New tools carry an internal/unreviewed label until their gates
    72	  and any claim they support are independently reviewed.
    73	
    74	Persistent avenue owners preserve depth. At every ideation round, rotating
    75	fresh-eyes lanes independently scan the whole campaign before receiving any
    76	narrower lens.
