   298	   combine compatible ideas, expose shared hidden assumptions, attack the
   299	   strongest proposal, and design the cheapest experiment that separates the
   300	   leading choices.
   301	6. **Run the canonical history/priority checksum.** Before compute, search
   302	   `AUDIT.md`, `APPROACHES.md`, `PROGRESS.md`, the newest `LIVE STATE`,
   303	   `ladder/REDUCTION.md`, and repository reports for every surviving target,
   304	   mechanism, and close synonym. Reconcile the master known-degree/closed-case
   305	   ledgers, then check each load-bearing literature claim in primary text.
   306	   Label every card `NEW`, `KNOWN`, `DUPLICATE`, or `SCOPE-CONFLICT` in the
   307	   synthesis. Blind consensus never overrides a banked exact result or primary
   308	   theorem; a shared stale packet premise is correlated error, not a vote.
   309	7. **Synthesize and launch.** The coordinator writes a ranked synthesis,
   310	   updates the avenue/claim graphs if needed, assigns owners and reviewers,
   311	   launches reversible lanes immediately, and records why alternatives were
   312	   deferred or stopped.  Deduplicate the systems checks, choose at most one
   313	   highest-value bounded upgrade for immediate work, and track it only in the
   314	   canonical `LIVE STATE` queue.  Trial at least one incremental machinery
   315	   improvement in every rolling 48-hour window unless no candidate clears its
   316	   measured benefit, regression-risk, and mathematical-opportunity-cost gate;
   317	   record a reasoned `NO_UPGRADE` rather than changing machinery for its own
   318	   sake.  Systems work runs beside, and normally does not block, live
   319	   mathematical research.
   320	
   321	Target 60 minutes for blind submissions, 30 for cross-pollination, and 30 for
   322	synthesis. Close a round within two hours when possible; if an ideator misses
   323	the close, mark the round `DEGRADED` instead of blocking ongoing research.
   324	Events arriving after the snapshot are queued for the next micro/full round
   325	and never silently mutate the sealed packet.
   326	
   327	Round artifacts use
   328	`xmodel/ideation-<YYYYMMDDTHHMMZ>-<lane>.md` and
   329	`xmodel/ideation-<YYYYMMDDTHHMMZ>-synthesis.md`.
   330	
   331	### External web sweep — at least every 24 hours
   332	
   333	No more than 24 hours may pass between completed broad sweeps. Low-cost alerts
   334	and known-actor watches run between sweeps when available. An external event
   335	can trigger both immediate intake and a full ideation round.
   336	
   337	The sweep covers broad phrase/concept searches as well as arXiv, repositories,
   338	Zenodo, MathOverflow, Palomar and its public discussion channels, relevant
   339	social feeds, citations, and the known-actor watchlist. Date-windowed searches
   340	are supplemental, because old but newly discovered artifacts have already
   341	escaped them.
   342	
   343	Classify an item `ACTIONABLE` only if it can change correctness, route rank,
   344	priority/publication posture, artifacts, or actor status. For each actionable
   345	item: preserve URL and timestamp, snapshot or hash the artifact, extract the
   346	exact claim without overreading it, replay the cheapest decisive check, map it
   347	to the claim DAG and avenue graph, and assign follow-up. Bank a negative sweep
   348	too; absence of a hit is weak evidence, not evidence of absence.
   349	
   350	### Classical frontier admissibility gate
   351	
   352	Before registering compute, every lane must state separately the actual total
   353	degrees, partial-`y` degrees, weighted degrees, and whether any total/
   354	coefficient-`x` cap is finite.  It must then reconcile that honest scope with
   355	the classical closed-case ledger and primary sources.  In particular, the
   356	Guccione--Guccione--Valqui/Heitmann theorem requires
   357	`gcd(deg_total P,deg_total Q) >= 16` for a characteristic-zero
   358	counterexample.  Thus every envelope with both total degrees at most `12`
   359	and every explicitly registered fixed actual-total pair such as `(9,12)` or
   360	`(8,12)` is counterexample-closed.  Historical `max12` and “maximum-12” tags
   361	normally name a maximum actual partial-`y`-degree frontier; they never
   362	establish a finite coefficient-`x` or total-degree cap.  Only an explicit
   363	actual-total pair or total cap licenses `METHOD_CONTROL_ONLY`; an unbounded-
   364	total partial-`y` lane remains `NOT_CLOSED_BY_THIS_GATE` unless another
   365	theorem closes its exact scope.
   366	
   367	For the mechanically covered cases, attach the deterministic output of
   368	`ops/frontier_gate.py` to `REGISTRATION.md`.  A
   369	`REFUSE_CLASSICALLY_CLOSED` verdict blocks frontier compute.  Such a lane may
   370	run only after being relabelled `method-control`, with a named live client and
   371	a strict cost/stop condition; its output cannot be advertised as advancing
   372	the closed degree frontier.  `NOT_CLOSED_BY_THIS_GATE` means only that this
   373	one theorem is inconclusive.  Unbounded-total partial-`y` work must say
   374	`--total-unbounded` explicitly and still pass every other classical/history
   375	check.  Any significant routing news reruns this gate across active lanes
   376	before further capacity is allocated.
   377	
   378	## Capacity allocation
   379	
   380	Default portfolio targets, adjusted when evidence demands it:
   381	
   382	- 35% strongest current critical path;
   383	- 20% new avenues and cross-avenue connections;
   384	- 20% adversarial review and replication;
   385	- 15% mathematical software, formalization, decisive-experiment design, and
   386	  bounded campaign-system improvement;
   387	- 5% external intelligence;
   388	- 5% state integration and publication readiness.
   389	
   390	With four reasoning slots, the usual shape is: coordinator/integrator;
   391	strongest current route; orthogonal new or disproof route; and
   392	risk-prioritized review/rapid response. Use wider model fleets for blind idea
   393	generation and independent review, and separate compute capacity from scarce
   394	reasoning slots. Do not leave all slots exploring descendants of one premise.
   395	
   396	Whenever provisional review debt exists, reserve at least one reasoning slot
   397	or 25% of research capacity (whichever is practical) for review and
   398	falsification. Two consecutive non-informative attempts on the same
   399	representation force a redesign; a third requires written justification. Two
   400	full rounds with unchanged leading gaps and no information gain trigger a
   401	zero-base fresh-eyes reset for one cycle.
   402	
   403	Choose work by expected information gain per unit time and cost, not by how
   404	many agents or tokens it consumes. Track event-to-decisive-test time, review
   405	latency/debt, central gaps resolved, provisional exposure and rollback cost,
   406	new connections actually tested, and information gained per compute dollar.
   407	For campaign machinery also track report-to-ingestion latency, stale or
   408	missing state, context bytes per lane, duplicate work prevented, adapter and
   409	job failure rates, model/fleet utilization, and time to a sealed replayable
   410	certificate.  Retain an upgrade only when those measurements or mathematical
   411	throughput improve without an offsetting reliability regression.
   412	
   413	## Tick, banking, and live state
   414	
   415	At each coordinator tick:
   416	
   417	1. read the newest `LIVE STATE` and any events since it;
   418	2. sweep local lanes and remote machines; verify exact process identities and
   419	   stop idle paid capacity within standing authority;
   420	3. rerun the classical frontier gate on new scopes or significant news;
   421	4. harvest finished work, apply the provisional gate, and start hostile review
   422	   immediately for promotable claims;
   423	5. propagate review outcomes through the claim DAG without blocking unrelated
   424	   work;
   425	6. test the 12-hour ideation and 24-hour sweep deadlines and all event triggers;
   426	7. rebalance the portfolio, launch the next bounded lanes, and assign a stop
   427	   condition to each;
   428	8. append findings, corrections, dead ends, costs, and decisions to `notes.md`,
   429	   then append a fresh `LIVE STATE` block.
   430	
   431	Before launch, check active tags, prior `xmodel/` reports, `AUDIT.md`, and
   432	`APPROACHES.md`. One question/deliverable has one live owner unless a second
   433	lane is explicitly registered as independent replication.
   434	
   435	Use this compact block; append rather than editing an old one:
   436	
   437	```text
   438	## <UTC timestamp> LIVE STATE
   439	- Basis: <commit and any explicitly dirty artifact hashes>
   440	- Coordinator / ideators: <active coordinator; full-round research roster>
   441	- Last full ideation: <UTC / round ID>; next deadline: <UTC>
   442	- Last broad web sweep: <UTC / report>; next deadline: <UTC>
   443	- Last system improvement/check: <UTC / result>; next 48-hour checkpoint: <UTC>
   444	- Active lanes: <tag, owner, inputs, stop condition>
   445	- Provisional claims: <ID, tier, parents, descendants, review>
   446	- Review queue/debt: <priority and due time>
   447	- Holds/human gates: <exact action and authority needed>
   448	- Top gaps: <links into APPROACHES/REDUCTION/AUDIT>
   449	- Immediate queue/triggers: <ranked bounded actions>
   450	```
   451	
   452	At the end of a calendar day, update that day's single `PROGRESS.md` entry.
   453	Negative results and superseded plans remain in `notes.md`; they prevent the
   454	campaign from paying twice for the same failed idea.
   455	
   456	## Replayability and operational safety
   457	
   458	- Computational claims ship engines, certificates, exact replay commands,
   459	  versions, input hashes, seeds, host, UTC times, and meaningful negative
   460	  controls. Mod-p work records every prime.
   461	- A claimed `python -O` or `-OO` verification is admissible only when every
   462	  load-bearing check remains live in that mode. Freeze an AST scan showing no
   463	  `Assert` nodes in the verification paths (or prove that any remaining
   464	  asserts are non-gating diagnostics), and run a deliberate old-pass/new-fail
   465	  mutation under every claimed interpreter mode. Byte-identical positive
   466	  output alone is insufficient: stripped checks can print the same answer
   467	  vacuously. Ordinary-only scripts may use `assert` only when the report labels
   468	  that limitation and makes no optimized-mode evidence claim.
   469	- A successor residual at digit `n` is typed only after an exact numerator `N`
   470	  is proved divisible by `p^n` on the charged predecessor scheme and
   471	  `N/p^n mod p` is derived with all lower-order divided carries retained. If
   472	  the quotient is not integral on that scheme, or generated coefficient rows
   473	  disagree with an exact determinant/source-identity reconstruction, the gate
   474	  is `TYPE-FAIL` and must not be used downstream.
   475	- msolve 0.10.1 characteristic-zero `-g` may return a first-machine-prime
   476	  unit basis before rational reconstruction while printing a characteristic-0
   477	  header. A char-0-header `[1]` is only first-prime trace evidence unless an
   478	  independently checked exact rational certificate is present. See `AUDIT.md`.
   479	- Run all heavy or uncertain-duration campaign computation on AWS, never on
   480	  the local machine. This includes CAS/solver jobs, Lean builds, and long or
   481	  potentially multi-GB exact-Python replays/enumerations. Reserve local
   482	  execution for editing, orchestration, hashing, status checks, model-review
   483	  adapters without compute tools, and genuinely short low-memory validation.
   484	  Follow `ops/FLEET.md` for machine inventory, shipping, caps, telemetry, and
   485	  kill safety.
   486	- `jc2-lean` is a separately owned nested repository and is outside the
   487	  campaign's inspection boundary. Campaign agents must not enter, enumerate,
   488	  search, read, build, status, modify, or control it. Scope every parent Git
   489	  query explicitly away from that path; never stage its gitlink. The parent
   490	  `.ignore` excludes it from ripgrep-style broad searches. Concurrent local
   491	  formalization may consume shared CPU/RAM, but campaign contention checks
   492	  remain system-level and must not identify or inspect that nested workload.
   493	- New heavy runners fail closed off AWS before importing a CAS or allocating
   494	  large objects, require a registered AWS job tag, and record the remote
   495	  hostname in custody.  New counterexample/frontier runners also record the
   496	  classical admissibility verdict described above before launch.  A
   497	  coordinator process-tree/swap-delta audit
   498	  is part of each live-state checkpoint; allocated swap without new pageouts
   499	  is historical occupancy, not by itself active thrashing.
   500	- A process-group guard is valid only if its recorded group includes the
   501	  actual CAS and every descendant whose RSS or lifetime it must control.
   502	  Wrappers that create an unrecorded inner PGID (including GNU `timeout`
   503	  without `--foreground`) are forbidden unless every inner group is itself
   504	  recorded and validated.  Before a new or repaired heavy runner launches,
   505	  a live no-CAS dummy regression must show that descendant RSS is included in
   506	  telemetry and that namespace-validated TERM, then KILL if needed, leaves no
   507	  nonzombie descendant or orphan; freeze that regression with the source.
   508	- Reviewed `ops/run_capped.py` is the opt-in `CAPRUN/v1` pilot for bounded
   509	  argv-only process groups. Its exact-PGID scope, inherited per-process CPU
   510	  limit, sampled RSS overshoot, and typed incomplete-cleanup outcome are
   511	  binding limitations. No caller migration is implicit; each migration needs
   512	  its own regression and review.
   513	- Third-party tools may mutate shared CLI configuration; adapters must isolate
   514	  or sanitize it, and a new/updated adapter gets a smoke test before use.
   515	- Lane launchers take prompt files, reject duplicate live tags, record their
   516	  true exit status, and keep one task and deliverable path per tag.  Every
   517	  model-review prompt names exactly one report path whose basename matches the
   518	  lane tag, explicitly instructs the reviewer to write that file and no other,
   519	  and is smoke-checked for that destination before launch.  Referee text left
   520	  only in adapter stdout is a failed-delivery draft, not promotion evidence;
   521	  preserve it and rerun through a fresh output-explicit prompt.
   522	- For a long external lane on macOS, prefer
   523	  `python3 ops/lane_detach.py launch ADAPTER TAG PROMPT`. It runs the unchanged
   524	  `ops/lane.sh` as a one-shot launchd job, so an accidental coordinator or
   525	  terminal-process death does not cancel model work. Monitor only with
   526	  `lane_detach.py status/wait` while live; those commands read a separate
   527	  ignored sidecar and launchd state, never the mutable report, model log, or
   528	  `.run.v2`. A terminal supervisor state merely licenses the existing
   529	  receipt-first procedure: reproduce the receipt and all charged hashes before
   530	  reading or binding the report. `unload` refuses live jobs and retains the
   531	  recovery sidecar. Direct foreground `ops/lane.sh` remains suitable for
   532	  short smoke tests whose exec session will be held to completion.
   533	- `ops/lane.sh` appends the compact current `FALLACY-v2.md` reasoning
   534	  guardrail exactly once from a hash-pinned private snapshot and records both
   535	  the original and composed prompt hashes.  The appendix is semantic
   536	  instruction, not a lexical proof checker.  Reports may declare an exact machine line
   537	  `charge_basis={...}`; the validator checks its rational delta, branch,
   538	  positive flag count, and citation.  Invalid declarations quarantine the
   539	  lane. The declaration is only for a newly asserted exit price: a report
   540	  with no such assertion must omit it, in which case `ABSENT` is the expected
   541	  receipt status and is never interpreted as a mathematical pass. Never add a
   542	  placeholder declaration for ordinary input hashes, geometry, or use of an
   543	  already promoted price. Changes to the prompt, appendix,
   544	  adapter, or validator during a run quarantine the result; focused launcher
   545	  regression is required after any edit to this path. Versioned predecessor
   546	  `FALLACY.md` remains immutable for packet replay.
   547	- A campaign win requires a global proof or an explicit characteristic-zero
   548	  counterexample at its honest evidence tier. Failure of selected formal
   549	  families to algebraize, or closure within one book/chart/degree range, is
   550	  not by itself a resolution of JC2.
   551	
   552	## Bootstrap for a fresh coordinator
   553	
   554	1. Read this file, then `README.md`, the newest `PROGRESS.md` entry, the
   555	   canonical-correction/current-state sections of `AUDIT.md`, and all of
   556	   `APPROACHES.md`.
   557	2. Read `notes.md` from the bottom through the newest `LIVE STATE` and all
   558	   later events. Historical `STRATEGY` and `STANDING QUEUE` blocks are
   559	   provenance, not current policy.
   560	3. Check the campaign repository's explicitly scoped status and basis commit,
   561	   excluding `jc2-lean` without inspecting it. Sweep exact local lane tags and
   562	   `ops/FLEET.md` machines; harvest before relaunching anything.
   563	4. Resolve overdue review, ideation, and web-sweep clocks. Continue the outer
   564	   loop. Never silently promote, publish, spend beyond authority, or discard
   565	   another lane's work.
