   251	### Full-spectrum ideation — at least every 12 hours
   252	
   253	No more than 12 hours may pass between completed full rounds. A significant
   254	event starts one sooner. Each round follows this protocol:
   255	
   256	1. **Freeze a state packet.** Record UTC time, clean basis commit, newer local
   257	   hashes if any, newest `LIVE STATE`, active/recent lane reports, review debt,
   258	   current `APPROACHES.md`, load-bearing `AUDIT.md` corrections, and all new
   259	   external evidence since the prior round.
   260	2. **Blind independent scan.** Every active research agent is a core ideator by
   261	   default and reads the whole avenue map, current gaps, and new evidence
   262	   before seeing the other submissions. A noninterruptible compute or review
   263	   worker may be omitted explicitly; mark the round degraded if this leaves
   264	   inadequate coverage. A rotating specialist lens may be added only after
   265	   the common scan. Model diversity is preferred; duplicate instances still
   266	   think independently.
   267	   **Every model marked as an equal-standing whole-portfolio researcher in the
   268	   roster** is invited automatically to every full round.  Each receives the
   269	   same sealed packet, submission contract, tool boundary, and deadline, and
   270	   must submit before seeing any other lane's report.  Every submission
   271	   receives equal post-deduplication consideration: model identity is neither
   272	   a bonus nor a vote, and operational unavailability degrades but does not
   273	   block the round.
   274	3. **Required submission contract.** Each report gives:
   275	   - a compact disposition vector over every numbered avenue: `unchanged`,
   276	     `raise`, `lower`, or `reopen`, with reasons for every change;
   277	   - a reranking of the principal proof and disproof bottlenecks;
   278	   - at least one genuinely new avenue or mechanism;
   279	   - at least one new connection between existing avenues;
   280	   - the strongest proof attack and strongest counterexample/falsification
   281	     attack;
   282	   - one software acceleration or decisive experiment;
   283	   - a short campaign-systems check, independent of the mathematical software
   284	     proposal: either an `UPGRADE` card with the smallest useful test or
   285	     implementation, or `NO_CHANGE` with evidence.  Rotate across state
   286	     freshness, context and retrieval cost, claim/review propagation,
   287	     duplication, model routing and utilization, adapter reliability, AWS
   288	     scheduling and cost, reproducibility, and operator/chat-summary quality;
   289	   - no more than three detailed idea cards, each with explicit dependencies,
   290	     cheapest discriminator, interpretation of each outcome, stop condition,
   291	     and expected information gain;
   292	   - a `continue / redesign / stop` recommendation for current major lanes.
   293	4. **Deduplicate after collection.** Fingerprint ideas by target obstruction,
   294	   mechanism, object, and decisive test. Merge operational duplicates while
   295	   preserving independent votes, disagreements, and genuinely different proof
   296	   mechanisms. Shared wording is not independent support.
   297	5. **Cross-pollinate adversarially.** Only after blind collection, ask lanes to
   298	   combine compatible ideas, expose shared hidden assumptions, attack the
   299	   strongest proposal, and design the cheapest experiment that separates the
   300	   leading choices.
   301	6. **Run the canonical history/priority checksum.** Before compute, search
   302	   `AUDIT.md`, `APPROACHES.md`, `PROGRESS.md`, the newest `LIVE STATE`,
   303	   `ladder/REDUCTION.md`, and repository reports for every surviving target,
   304	   mechanism, and close synonym. Reconcile the master known-degree/closed-case
   305	   ledgers, then check each load-bearing literature claim in primary text.
   306	   Label every card `NEW`, `KNOWN`, `DUPLICATE`, or `SCOPE-CONFLICT` in the
   307	   synthesis. Blind consensus never overrides a banked exact result or primary
   308	   theorem; a shared stale packet premise is correlated error, not a vote.
   309	7. **Synthesize and launch.** The coordinator writes a ranked synthesis,
   310	   updates the avenue/claim graphs if needed, assigns owners and reviewers,
   311	   launches reversible lanes immediately, and records why alternatives were
   312	   deferred or stopped.  Deduplicate the systems checks, choose at most one
   313	   highest-value bounded upgrade for immediate work, and track it only in the
   314	   canonical `LIVE STATE` queue.  Trial at least one incremental machinery
   315	   improvement in every rolling 48-hour window unless no candidate clears its
   316	   measured benefit, regression-risk, and mathematical-opportunity-cost gate;
   317	   record a reasoned `NO_UPGRADE` rather than changing machinery for its own
   318	   sake.  Systems work runs beside, and normally does not block, live
   319	   mathematical research.
   320	
   321	Target 60 minutes for blind submissions, 30 for cross-pollination, and 30 for
   322	synthesis. Close a round within two hours when possible; if an ideator misses
   323	the close, mark the round `DEGRADED` instead of blocking ongoing research.
   324	Events arriving after the snapshot are queued for the next micro/full round
   325	and never silently mutate the sealed packet.
   326	
   327	Round artifacts use
   328	`xmodel/ideation-<YYYYMMDDTHHMMZ>-<lane>.md` and
   329	`xmodel/ideation-<YYYYMMDDTHHMMZ>-synthesis.md`.
   330	
   331	### External web sweep — at least every 24 hours
   332	
   333	No more than 24 hours may pass between completed broad sweeps. Low-cost alerts
   334	and known-actor watches run between sweeps when available. An external event
   335	can trigger both immediate intake and a full ideation round.
   336	
   337	The sweep covers broad phrase/concept searches as well as arXiv, repositories,
   338	Zenodo, MathOverflow, Palomar and its public discussion channels, relevant
   339	social feeds, citations, and the known-actor watchlist. Date-windowed searches
   340	are supplemental, because old but newly discovered artifacts have already
   341	escaped them.
   342	
   343	Classify an item `ACTIONABLE` only if it can change correctness, route rank,
   344	priority/publication posture, artifacts, or actor status. For each actionable
   345	item: preserve URL and timestamp, snapshot or hash the artifact, extract the
   346	exact claim without overreading it, replay the cheapest decisive check, map it
   347	to the claim DAG and avenue graph, and assign follow-up. Bank a negative sweep
   348	too; absence of a hit is weak evidence, not evidence of absence.
   349	
   350	### Classical frontier admissibility gate
   351	
   352	Before registering compute, every lane must state separately the actual total
   353	degrees, partial-`y` degrees, weighted degrees, and whether any total/
   354	coefficient-`x` cap is finite.  It must then reconcile that honest scope with
   355	the classical closed-case ledger and primary sources.  In particular, the
   356	Guccione--Guccione--Valqui/Heitmann theorem requires
   357	`gcd(deg_total P,deg_total Q) >= 16` for a characteristic-zero
   358	counterexample.  Thus every envelope with both total degrees at most `12`
   359	and every explicitly registered fixed actual-total pair such as `(9,12)` or
   360	`(8,12)` is counterexample-closed.  Historical `max12` and “maximum-12” tags
   361	normally name a maximum actual partial-`y`-degree frontier; they never
   362	establish a finite coefficient-`x` or total-degree cap.  Only an explicit
   363	actual-total pair or total cap licenses `METHOD_CONTROL_ONLY`; an unbounded-
   364	total partial-`y` lane remains `NOT_CLOSED_BY_THIS_GATE` unless another
   365	theorem closes its exact scope.
   366	
   367	For the mechanically covered cases, attach the deterministic output of
   368	`ops/frontier_gate.py` to `REGISTRATION.md`.  A
   369	`REFUSE_CLASSICALLY_CLOSED` verdict blocks frontier compute.  Such a lane may
   370	run only after being relabelled `method-control`, with a named live client and
   371	a strict cost/stop condition; its output cannot be advertised as advancing
   372	the closed degree frontier.  `NOT_CLOSED_BY_THIS_GATE` means only that this
   373	one theorem is inconclusive.  Unbounded-total partial-`y` work must say
   374	`--total-unbounded` explicitly and still pass every other classical/history
   375	check.  Any significant routing news reruns this gate across active lanes
   376	before further capacity is allocated.
   377	
   378	## Capacity allocation
   379	
   380	Default portfolio targets, adjusted when evidence demands it:
   381	
   382	- 35% strongest current critical path;
   383	- 20% new avenues and cross-avenue connections;
   384	- 20% adversarial review and replication;
   385	- 15% mathematical software, formalization, decisive-experiment design, and
   386	  bounded campaign-system improvement;
   387	- 5% external intelligence;
   388	- 5% state integration and publication readiness.
   389	
   390	With four reasoning slots, the usual shape is: coordinator/integrator;
   391	strongest current route; orthogonal new or disproof route; and
   392	risk-prioritized review/rapid response. Use wider model fleets for blind idea
   393	generation and independent review, and separate compute capacity from scarce
   394	reasoning slots. Do not leave all slots exploring descendants of one premise.
   395	
   396	Whenever provisional review debt exists, reserve at least one reasoning slot
   397	or 25% of research capacity (whichever is practical) for review and
   398	falsification. Two consecutive non-informative attempts on the same
   399	representation force a redesign; a third requires written justification. Two
   400	full rounds with unchanged leading gaps and no information gain trigger a
   401	zero-base fresh-eyes reset for one cycle.
   402	
   403	Choose work by expected information gain per unit time and cost, not by how
   404	many agents or tokens it consumes. Track event-to-decisive-test time, review
   405	latency/debt, central gaps resolved, provisional exposure and rollback cost,
   406	new connections actually tested, and information gained per compute dollar.
   407	For campaign machinery also track report-to-ingestion latency, stale or
   408	missing state, context bytes per lane, duplicate work prevented, adapter and
   409	job failure rates, model/fleet utilization, and time to a sealed replayable
   410	certificate.  Retain an upgrade only when those measurements or mathematical
   411	throughput improve without an offsetting reliability regression.
   412	
   413	## Tick, banking, and live state
   414	
   415	At each coordinator tick:
   416	
   417	1. read the newest `LIVE STATE` and any events since it;
   418	2. sweep local lanes and remote machines; verify exact process identities and
   419	   stop idle paid capacity within standing authority;
   420	3. rerun the classical frontier gate on new scopes or significant news;
   421	4. harvest finished work, apply the provisional gate, and start hostile review
   422	   immediately for promotable claims;
   423	5. propagate review outcomes through the claim DAG without blocking unrelated
   424	   work;
   425	6. test the 12-hour ideation and 24-hour sweep deadlines and all event triggers;
   426	7. rebalance the portfolio, launch the next bounded lanes, and assign a stop
   427	   condition to each;
   428	8. append findings, corrections, dead ends, costs, and decisions to `notes.md`,
   429	   then append a fresh `LIVE STATE` block.
   430	

