    90	nonempty and divisorial.
    91	
    92	## 3. Generic companion sheets
    93	
    94	For every irreducible component `D=V(p_D)` of `B`, the polynomial
    95	`p_D(F,G)` is nonzero and nonconstant.  Some component of its zero curve
    96	dominates `D`; all its points lie in `j(A2)`, disjoint from `R`.  Hence the
    97	generic fibre above `D` contains at least one unramified factor.  If its residue
    98	degree is `f>1`, geometric inertia fixes `f` sheets; no false globally labelled
    99	sheet is asserted.
