   126	No strict intermediate field, `d1>=2`, surjectivity of `j`, or etaleness of
   127	`j` beyond its open-immersion property is used here.
   128	
   129	## 5. Rank-three source-to-target topology
   130	
   131	Assume for contradiction that `[L:K]=3`.  A non-etale point in a closed fibre
   132	of `pi` consumes local fibre length at least two.  Since the total length is
   133	three, every branch value has exactly one reduced non-etale source point.
   134	Therefore
   135	
   136	```text
   137	R -> B
   138	```
   139	
   140	is finite point-bijective and is a homeomorphism on complex analytic spaces;
   141	it need not be a scheme isomorphism.
   142	
   143	Moreover `R` lies in the boundary `Y-j(A2)`.  Approaching it through the dense
   144	source chart produces an escaping source sequence with convergent `F`-image,
   145	so `B subset A(F)`.  The finite image of each irreducible `R` component is a
   146	curve and therefore an entire irreducible component of the plane curve `A(F)`.
   147	Chau's published theorem polynomially parametrizes each such component.  Its
   148	normalization, and the normalization of the corresponding `R` component, is
   149	`A1`.
