   151	Resolving affine multibranch points retains self-branches and parallel edges
   152	in the component/singular-point incidence multigraph.  That graph is a minor
   153	or subdivision of the completion-boundary forest and is therefore a forest.
   154	Normalization additivity then gives
   155	
   156	```text
   157	e_c(B)=e_c(R)=b0(R)=b0(B)=h>=1.                        (5.1)
   158	```
   159	
   160	## 6. The unique Euler row
   161	
   162	Let `S0=A2-pi(U)`.  Generic companion sheets make `S0` finite.  The only cubic
   163	fibre rows are
   164	
   165	```text
   166	off B:  (1,1,1), u=3;      B-S0: (2,1), u=1;
   167	S0:     (3),     u=0.
   168	```
