   174	```
   175	
   176	Combining (6.1) with (4.1), the `C=P1` equation
   177	`2h+|S0|+Q=1` is impossible.  The `C=A1` equation has the unique solution
   178	
   179	```text
   180	C=A1,        h=1,        S0=empty,        Q=0.          (6.2)
   181	```
   182	
   183	Thus `B` is connected and its affine-line component incidence is a forest, so
   184	`B` is topologically contractible.  Because `S0` is empty, every branch value
   185	has a local length-one factor; finite-flat idempotent splitting over the
   186	henselian base makes it a rank-one henselian companion.
   187	
   188	## 7. Monodromy contradiction
   189	
   190	Over `A2-B`, the degree-three cover is connected and finite etale, so its
   191	monodromy is transitive.  Normality gives nonidentity generic inertia.  With a
   192	fixed companion sheet, generic inertia is a transposition.
   193	
   194	Arzhantsev--Zaidenberg classify every reduced connected simply connected plane
   195	curve into the comb/line and weighted-cone families.  In the comb family the
   196	spine meridian is central; its transposition centralizer preserves the fixed
   197	sheet and is intransitive.  In the weighted-cone family the origin henselian
   198	companion splits analytically, and a weighted sublevel inside its ordinary
   199	splitting ball retracts radially onto the global complement.  The global image
   200	therefore lies in a point stabilizer and is again intransitive.  Both contradict
   201	connected-cover transitivity, proving (0.1).
