   179	## 3. Conductor-six one-place delta-sequences
   180	
   181	For a delta-sequence `(r0,...,rh)`, put
   182	
   183	```text
   184	d1=r0,       d_(i+1)=gcd(r0,...,ri),       e_i=d_i/d_(i+1).
   185	```
   186	
   187	The Assi--Garcia-Sanchez conductor formula is
   188	
   189	```text
   190	mu=sum_(i=1)^h (e_i-1)r_i-r0+1.                         (3.1)
   191	```
   192	
   193	Here `mu=2g=6`.  Their fixed-genus bound gives `h<=log2(g+1)=2`.
   194	
   195	If `h=1`, (3.1) is
   196	
   197	```text
   198	(r0-1)(r1-1)=6,
   199	```
   200	
   201	and `r0>r1`, coprimality give
   202	
   203	```text
   204	(r0,r1)=(7,2),(4,3).                                   (3.2)
   205	```
   206	
   207	Now let `h=2`, put
   208	
   209	```text
   210	d=d2,       r0=a*d,       r1=b*d.
   211	```
   212	
   213	The delta inequalities give `a>b>=2`, `gcd(a,b)=1`, and `d>=2`.  Freeness
   214	at the last step says
   215	
   216	```text
   217	d*r2 in <r0,r1>,       equivalently r2 in <a,b>,        (3.3)
   218	```
   219	
   220	so `r2>=b>=2`.  Formula (3.1) becomes
   221	
   222	```text
   223	6=d*((a-1)b-a)+(d-1)r2+1.                              (3.4)
   224	```
   225	
   226	Since
   227	
   228	```text
   229	(a-1)b-a=(a-1)(b-1)-1>=1,
   230	```
   231	
   232	(3.4) gives `3d-1<=6`, hence `d=2`.  It follows that
   233	
   234	```text
   235	2*((a-1)b-a)+r2=5.
   236	```
   237	
   238	The only solution under the displayed bounds is
   239	
   240	```text
   241	(a,b,r2)=(3,2,3),       (r0,r1,r2)=(6,4,3).            (3.5)
   242	```
   243	
   244	Thus the complete conductor-six list is
   245	
   246	```text
   247	(7,2),       (4,3),       (6,4,3).                     (3.6)
   248	```
   249	
   250	Under the standard Puiseux/cabling dictionary, the first two are the torus
   251	rows `T(2,7)` and `T(3,4)`.  In (3.5), the first gcd drop gives the trefoil
   252	`T(3,2)` and the final drop has winding two and meridional absolute value
