   267	## 4. Complete `(6,4,3)` parametrization normal form
   268	
   269	Let `A=C[U(t),V(t)]` be the coordinate ring of a rational polynomial curve
   270	with delta-sequence `(6,4,3)`.  The reduced-coordinate/approximate-root
   271	construction gives
   272	
   273	```text
   274	deg U=4,       deg V=6,
   275	```
   276	
   277	and a weighted Weierstrass approximate root of parameter degree three.
   278	Completing the square in `V`, depressing the cubic in `U`, scaling leading
   279	coefficients, and translating the parameter are allowed polynomial target
   280	automorphisms and an affine automorphism of `A1`.  They reduce the root to
   281	
   282	```text
   283	V^2-U^3+A*U+B,                                          (4.1)
   284	```
   285	
   286	and the parametrization to
   287	
   288	```text
   289	U=t^4+a2*t^2+a1*t+a0,
   290	V=t^6+b4*t^4+b3*t^3+b2*t^2+b1*t+b0.                    (4.2)
   291	```
   292	
   293	For (4.1) to have degree three, coefficients of `V^2-U^3` in degrees ten
   294	through five must vanish; its degree-four coefficient is cancelled by
   295	`A*U`.  Direct coefficient comparison gives
   296	
   297	```text
   298	b4=3a2/2,
   299	b3=3a1/2,
   300	b2=3(4a0+a2^2)/8,
   301	b1=3a1*a2/4,
   302	b0=(12a0*a2+6a1^2-a2^3)/16,                            (4.3)
   303	
   304	[t^5](V^2-U^3)=-3a1(4a0-a2^2)/8.                       (4.4)
   305	```
   306	
   307	If `a1=0`, canceling the degree-four term with `A*U` leaves no degree-three
   308	term, contradicting `r2=3`.  Therefore `a1=c!=0`, and (4.4) forces
   309	
   310	```text
   311	a0=a2^2/4.
   312	```
   313	
   314	Writing `h=a2/2`, equations (4.2)--(4.3) are exactly (0.4).  Conversely,
   315	direct expansion gives the required approximate root
   316	
   317	```text
   318	V^2-U^3-(3/4)c^2*h*U
   319	  =(c^3/64)(8t^3+24h*t+9c),                            (4.5)
   320	```
   321	
   322	of degree three.  Thus (0.4) is not one convenient example; it is the full
   323	normalized row.
   324	
   325	There is no hidden cusp in this family.  Exact elimination gives
   326	
   327	```text
   328	Res_t(U'(t),V'(t))=-1728*c^5 !=0.                       (4.6)
   329	```
   330	
   331	Hence the normalization map is immersive for every allowed `c` and `h`.
