    89	## 2. Normal form and total affine delta
    90	
    91	Let the two coordinate functions supplied by the one-stage delta sequence
    92	have degrees three and four.  Translate the affine parameter to kill the
    93	quadratic term of the cubic, scale and translate the first target coordinate,
    94	and obtain
    95	
    96	```text
    97	X=t^3+a*t.
    98	```
    99	
   100	Scale and translate the second target coordinate, then subtract a scalar
   101	multiple of `X` to kill its cubic term.  This gives (0.1).  All operations are
   102	affine automorphisms of the normalization or target; they preserve the
   103	normalization fibres and the charged topology.
   104	
   105	The two pole orders at `t=infinity` are coprime, so
   106	`C(X,Y)=C(t)` and the parametrization is birational.  Homogenizing to degree
   107	four gives
   108	
   109	```text
   110	[T:S] |->
   111	[T^3*S+a*T*S^3 : T^4+b*T^2*S^2+c*T*S^3 : S^4].       (2.1)
   112	```
   113	
   114	There is one point at infinity, `[0:1:0]`.  In the chart where the middle
   115	coordinate is one and `r=S/T`, the first local coordinate is
   116	
   117	```text
   118	(r+a*r^3)/(1+b*r^2+c*r^3)=r+O(r^3),                  (2.2)
   119	```
   120	
   121	so the quartic is smooth there.  Its arithmetic genus is three and its
   122	normalization has genus zero.  Hence
   123	
   124	```text
   125	sum_(finite z) delta_z(B)=3.                           (2.3)
   126	```
