    62	four subgroup,
    63	
    64	```text
    65	M=Omega^V4,             Gal(M/K)=S3,
    66	K2=Omega^A4=M^A3,       Gal(K2/K)=C2.                  (2.1)
    67	```
    68	
    69	In the charged row every irreducible branch component is generically
    70	transposition-branched.  If `q_B` is the product of its distinct irreducible
    71	equations, factoriality of `C[x,y]` and the absence of a nontrivial etale
    72	quadratic cover of `A2` give
    73	
    74	```text
    75	K2=K(sqrt(q_B)).                                         (2.2)
    76	```
    77	
    78	The hypersurface
    79	
    80	```text
    81	D=Spec C[x,y,s]/(s^2-q_B)                               (2.3)
    82	```
    83	
    84	is a domain, is `S2`, and is regular in codimension one because `q_B` is
    85	reduced; hence it is normal and is the integral normalization in `K2`.
    86	Normalizing the affine plane in `M` gives connected `W`, and quotienting by
    87	`A3` gives the finite cyclic map `W->D`.
