    95	## 3. Complete point-stabilizer table
    96	
    97	For a closed target point, let `H_z<=S3` be the complete local decomposition
    98	group at a chosen point of `W`.  All closed residue fields are `C`; the
    99	stabilizer for the `A3` action in `W->D` is literally
   100	
   101	```text
   102	H_z intersect A3.                                       (3.1)
   103	```
   104	
   105	The two reviews independently reconstructed
   106	
   107	```text
   108	quartic fibre   image H_z in S3       H_z intersect A3
   109	(2,1,1)         C2                    1
   110	(2,2)           C2                    1
   111	(3,1)           S3                    A3
   112	(4)             A3 or S3              nontrivial.       (3.2)
   113	```
   114	
   115	At `(2,2)`, the two disjoint quartic transpositions have the same image in
   116	`S4/V4`; at `(3,1)`, transitivity on three sheets plus a generic
   117	transposition forces `S3`.  The corrected local `(4)` possibilities are
   118	`A4,S4`, not `D4`.
