+## 8. Degree-Eight AWS Decision
+
+Decision: yes, but only as bounded reconnaissance and pattern mining.  The cost
+is justified because the cell is small, the degree-six cell closed by a very
+sharp coefficient identity, and the packet reports 13 basis elements, 20
+parameters, and 57 equations.  It is not justified as a proof attempt for the
+full one-cusp horn.
+
+Exact job specification:
+
+- Coefficient ring: start over `Z` from the generated invariant pullback basis
+  `m_1,...,m_13` for `(mu,r)=(2,2)` and pullback degree `<=8`; normalized pair
+  `H1,H2` has 20 parameters after target affine normalization.  Work over
+  `Q` only for final lifted certificates; modular rings are
+  `F_p[c_1,...,c_20]`.
+- Term orders: first graded reverse lexicographic for ideal-shape and tangent
+  ranks; then lex/block order
+  `(Jacobian coefficient variables/elimination outputs) > (parameters)` for
+  parameter-independent coefficient identities; separately a field-degree
+  elimination order with `T` for the minimal polynomial of `X`.
+- Modular primes: `32003`, `65521`, `104729`, `131071`, `262147`, skipping any
+  prime that divides a generated denominator or degenerates the invariant-ring
+  relation.  At least two good primes must agree before any char-zero lift.
+- Saturation: saturate by the determinant of the normalized linear target
+  block, the nonzero constant Jacobian target, declared basis-normalization
+  pivots, and all localization factors used to define the cell.  Record the
+  ideal component before and after each saturation; run positive and negative
+  controls.
+- Split/shard strategy: shard by prime and by term-order task.  Each shard
+  emits the basis hash, ideal hash, saturation list, monomial order, engine
+  version, prime, wall/RSS telemetry, and a deterministic reduced output hash.
+  Keep Box01 on its existing GB21 work; use idle `r6*` nodes first.
+- Mutation controls: target constant `3` instead of `2`; drop one Jacobian
+  coefficient equation; remove the saturation by the linear determinant; and
+  perturb one basis monomial.  Each mutation must be detected.
+- Stopping rule: stop early if two primes show a positive-dimensional generic
+  component with no stable syzygy and no parameter-independent coefficient
