+  theorem to ask which branch components can be forced one-place, simple, or
+  transposition-branched.  If those hypotheses are unavailable, label them
+  `OPEN`.
+- Primitive/no-proper-block field extensions: the rank-four proper-block
+  theorem does not touch primitive cases.  The block-sandwich surface and
+  primitive monodromy lanes should continue independently.
+- Coefficient realization: K00 and formal-germ routes remain disproof-facing
+  because a nonempty family that algebraizes could still be a counterexample.
+  Require route-to-state provenance and normal-form quotient controls.
+- Reduction mod `p`: finite witnesses and positive components are not lifts.
+  A complete fixed-support all-depth lift plus determinant rows can imply a
+  complex collision by compactness; changing support cannot.
+- Valuation/formal maps: `A_infinity` should be attacked through valued initial
+  multiplicities and exact finite support discriminators, not generic tropical
+  slogans.
+- Bounded searches: useful only when source-derived and bounded by a theorem
+  interface, as in the D8 invariant-ring cell.  Random sparse search remains a
+  bug-hunt unless it comes with a fixed support and collision algebraization
+  bridge.
